\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Information flow of the GT-conditioned CVAE. \emph  {Top (Training):} the GT encoder and the posterior head are the only modules that consume the ground-truth volume $Y$; the decoder always renders from the sparse context features, so $z$ is the \emph  {sole} channel of dense/target information. The loss combines posterior reconstruction with the annealed, free-bits-floored $\mathrm  {KL}[q\|p]$ and an optional prior-reconstruction term. \emph  {Bottom (Deployment):} the GT encoder and posterior are removed; $N{=}8$ samples $z_n\sim p(z\mid C)$ from the same sparse-view prior yield a mean volume and per-point variance.}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:p5_flow}{{1}{10}{}{figure.1}{}}
\citation{lin2024difgaussian}
